Yes, you can make the link clickable in LaTeX by using the hyperref package. Here's an example:

\usepackage{hyperref}
...
Random sample consensus. (2021, September 9). In \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_sample_consensus}{Wikipedia}. Retrieved September 14, 2021, from \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_sample_consensus}

This will create a clickable hyperlink for the title "Wikipedia" and the URL, which will direct the reader to the Wikipedia page when clicked.
